/-!
# Morphisms into Proj

Let `S` be a graded ring and `X = Proj(S)`. For an integer `d` the open subscheme
`U_d = ⋃_{f ∈ S_d} D₊(f) ⊆ X` carries invertible twists `𝒪_X(nd)` whose multiplication maps
are isomorphisms. A morphism `φ : Y ⟶ X` through `U_d` therefore pulls the canonical graded
map `S → ⨁_n Γ(X, 𝒪_X(n))` back to a graded map out of the Veronese subring `S^{(d)}`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismsIntoProj.psiPullbackHom`: the degree-`n` component
  `S_{nd} → Γ(Y, φ⁎𝒪_X(nd))` of the map `ψ^d_φ`, and
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismsIntoProj.psiPullbackVeroneseHom`, the same map with the
  degree-`n` piece `(S^{(d)})_n` of the Veronese subring as its source.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismsIntoProj.isGoodOpen_degreeOpen`: `U_d` is a good open in
  the sense of Tag 01MU, so every twist `𝒪(nd)` restricts to an invertible sheaf on it and
  every multiplication map `𝒪(nd) ⊗ 𝒪(md) → 𝒪(nd + md)` restricts to an isomorphism.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismsIntoProj.generatesStalks_psiPullbackVeroneseHom_one`:
  **the global generation clause of Tag 01N7.** The invertible sheaf `φ⁎𝒪_X(d)` is generated by
  the global sections in the image of `(S^{(d)})_1 = S_d → Γ(Y, φ⁎𝒪_X(d))`. Its two inputs are
  `nonvanishingLocus_psiPullbackHom_one`, the nonvanishing locus of a degree-one value, and
  `isInvertibleModule_pullbackTwist_one`, invertibility of `φ⁎𝒪_X(d)`.

## Implementation notes

The target of `psiPullbackHom` is `Γ(Y, φ⁎𝒪_X(nd))` rather than the degree-`n` piece
`Γ(Y, (φ⁎𝒪_X(d))^{⊗ n})` of `Γ_*(Y, φ⁎𝒪_X(d))`, so the graded ring map that
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismsIntoProjGradedRing` assembles from `psiPullbackVeroneseHom`
is the twist-model form of Tag 01N7. The faithful form, with target the section ring of Tag 01CV
of `φ⁎𝒪_{U_d}(d)`, is `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismsIntoProj.psiPullbackSectionRing_spec` in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismsIntoProjSectionRing`, and it carries the tag.

Identifying the two is now possible. The isomorphism `𝒪_{U_d}(d)^{⊗ n} ≅ 𝒪_{U_d}(nd)` is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTwistTensorPowDegreeOpen.thetaNat`, assembled from the
multiplication isomorphisms of `isGoodOpen_degreeOpen`, and pulling it back along `φ` is
`Stacks.RelativeVeryAmple.pullbackTensorPowModuleIso` composed with it. An earlier note here
said the restriction functor to an open subscheme is not known to be monoidal; that is false.
Restriction to an open is pullback along the open immersion, Tag 01CD at scheme level is
`Stacks.RelativeVeryAmple.pullbackTensorModulesIso`, and
`Stacks.PullbackTensorCoherence.pullbackTensorComparison_associator` — with its unitor
companions — shows `f⁎` to be monoidal with the canonical comparison as its tensorator.

The existing declarations are left as they stand, since the degreewise maps with the twist as
target are what the consumers of this file use; the faithful form of Tag 01N7 is beside them, in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismsIntoProjSectionRing`.

**The global generation clause of Tag 01N7 does not wait on any of that**, and is proved below:
it is a statement about the degree-one piece alone, where the twist model and the tensor-power
model agree on the nose. The nonvanishing locus of the pullback of a global section is the
inverse image of its nonvanishing locus by Tag 0H78
(`Stacks.NonvanishingPullback.preimage_nonvanishingLocus`), the nonvanishing locus of the section
of `𝒪(d)` attached to `f ∈ S_d` is `D₊(f)` on the invertible locus by Tag 01MV
(`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CommonDegreeTwist.mem_nonvanishingLocus_degreeSection_iff'`), and
`φ` lands in `U_d = ⋃_{f ∈ S_d} D₊(f)`, so the inverse images of the `D₊(f)` cover `Y`. For an
invertible sheaf a nonvanishing germ generates the stalk
(`Stacks.SectionProduct.exists_smul_Γgerm`), and `φ⁎𝒪_X(d)` is invertible because
`𝒪_{U_d}(d)` is — `isGoodOpen_degreeOpen` — and the inverse image of an invertible sheaf is
invertible by Tag 0B8L.

**`thetaNat` is now multiplicative in every bidegree.** The square relating the addition law of
the tensor powers of `𝒪_{U_d}(d)` to the canonical multiplication of the twists is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ThetaMul.thetaNat_mul`, for arbitrary natural numbers `n` and `m`, with
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ThetaMul.theta_mul` the same statement at the degrees `d · n`; the
positive bidegrees come from the two associativity constraints
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ThetaMul.thetaStepNat_assoc` and `twistMulIsoNat_assoc` and the bidegree
`(n, 0)` from the two right unit laws `tensorPowModuleAddIso_zero_right` and
`twistMulIso_zero_right`. So the earlier note here, that the upgrade waits on the general-bidegree
compatibility and that unitality of the twist multiplication is unrecorded, is stale on both
counts.

The honest target is `Stacks.GradedSections.sectionRing` of `φ⁎𝒪_{U_d}(d)`, a graded commutative
ring by `Stacks.SectionRingGeometric.schemeSectionCommRing` with no further structure. Its product
is `Stacks.GradedSections.mul`, written through the addition law `Stacks.GradedSections.powAdd` of
the left-iterated powers by `Stacks.GradedSections.mul_eq`, on global sections by
`Stacks.SectionProduct.globalSection_mul` and on honest sections by
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjChartFromRatios.mulSections_globalSection`. On one scheme the two
addition laws now meet: `powAdd` is `AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.tensorPowAddIso` in
nonnegative degree, by `Stacks.GradedSections.powAddIso_hom` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.tensorPowAddIso_natCast`, and that is
`Stacks.Ample.tensorPowModuleAddIso` conjugated by the comparison of the two tensor products, by
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ThetaMul.addIsoSheaf_hom`.

**The pullback half of the square now holds.**
`Stacks.RelativeVeryAmple.pullbackTensorPowModuleIso_tensorPowModuleAddIso` says that
`Stacks.RelativeVeryAmple.pullbackTensorPowModuleIso` carries `Stacks.Ample.tensorPowModuleAddIso`
to the multiplication of the powers of the pullback, in every pair of nonnegative degrees. The
earlier note here — that this square exists only for
`Stacks.TensorPowerPullbackMul.pullbackPowModulesIso` and `powModulesAdd`, and that the monoidal
structure localizing the objectwise tensor product would have to be identified with the one whose
unit is `SheafOfModules.unit` first — is stale. The square is stated with the tensor product sheaf
of Tag 01CA, which is already the source of `tensorPowModuleAddIso` and both the source and target
of `Stacks.RelativeVeryAmple.pullbackTensorModulesIso`, so the powers of Tag 01CU enter only as
objects carrying a multiplication and no identification of structures is needed.

**The two descriptions of a global section of a pullback now meet.**
`Stacks.PullbackUnitSection.pullbackSectionHom_globalSection` says that for `f : 𝟙 ⟶ M` the
pullback of the global section of `f` along `j` — the unit of `j^* ⊣ j_*` evaluated on sections,
which is what `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjChartRatioPullback.pullSection` is built from — is the
global section of `Stacks.PullbackUnitSection.unitPullback j ≫ j^*f`, a morphism out of the
monoidal unit again. Its content is the degree zero case
`Stacks.PullbackUnitSection.globalSection_unitPullback`: the structure-sheaf comparison of Tag
01CD carries the pullback of the section `1` to `1`. So a square of module morphisms can now be
evaluated on the sections the degreewise map produces, and the earlier note here — that nothing
identified the two — is stale.

**The faithful form is proved**, in `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.MorphismsIntoProjSectionRing`,
and neither half of multiplicativity is missing any more. The *source* half — Tag 01N6 in the
tensor-power model — is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjDegreeOpenUniversalTriple.universalVeroneseSections`, whose
multiplicativity is `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ThetaMul.thetaNat_mul` read on the sections attached
to homogeneous elements. The *pullback* half is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjChartPullbackCotensorator.pullSection_mulSections`, packaged as
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTriplePullback.pullbackSections`. Both are stated for the product
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjChartFromRatios.mulSections` of honest global sections, which
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjChartFromRatios.mulSections_globalSection` identifies with the
product `Stacks.GradedSections.mul` of the section ring, so no transport of coherences between
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ThetaMul.schemeMonoidal` and
`Stacks.SheafInternalHom.schemeMonoidalCategory` is needed. The unit axiom is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTripleUnitSection.toFun_zero_eq_unitGlobal`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Equation 01N5](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01N5)
* [Stacks Project, Equation 01N7](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01N7)
